From: GameShellNeo project
Subject: [PATCH] brcmfmac: recover control RX allocation failures

Flush and request retransmission when a control response cannot be
allocated after its header was consumed. Preserve any already-published
response and count the failed receive. A successful NAK must clear the
next-frame hint: the retransmitted frame needs a new header read. Keep
normal next-frame hints when no retransmission was requested.

Isolated candidate after 0046 and 0047; no image integration.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c
@@ -1827,8 +1827,11 @@
 	brcmf_dbg(SDIO, "Enter\n");
 	if (bus->rxblen)
 		buf = vzalloc(bus->rxblen);
-	if (!buf)
+	if (!buf) {
+		bus->sdcnt.rxc_errors++;
+		brcmf_sdio_rxfail(bus, false, true);
 		goto done;
+	}
 
 	rbuf = bus->rxbuf;
 	pad = ((unsigned long)rbuf % bus->head_align);
@@ -1983,8 +1986,8 @@
 				brcmf_sdio_read_control(bus, bus->rxhdr,
 							rd->len,
 							rd->dat_offset);
-				/* prepare the descriptor for the next read */
-				rd->len = rd->len_nxtfrm << 4;
+				/* A retransmitted control frame needs a fresh header. */
+				rd->len = bus->rxskip ? 0 : rd->len_nxtfrm << 4;
 				rd->len_nxtfrm = 0;
 				/* treat all packet as event if we don't know */
 				rd->channel = SDPCM_EVENT_CHANNEL;
